(2) Rules and regulations for on-site sewage management systems (adopted by the department of public health and the county board of health and being chapter 511-3-1 as subsequently amended and updated), and policies of the county board of health pertaining to on-site sewage management systems;
(3) Rules and regulations for mass gatherings (adopted by the department of public and the county board of health and being chapter 511-3-2 as subsequently amended and updated), and policies of the county board of health pertaining to mass gatherings;
(4) Rules and regulations pertaining to drinking water supply (adopted by the department of public health and the county board of health and being chapter 511-3-3 as subsequently amended and updated), and policies of the county board of health pertaining to drinking water supply;
(5) Rules and regulations pertaining to solid waste (adopted by the department of public health and the county board of health and being chapter 511-3-4 as subsequently amended and updated), and policies of the county board of health pertaining to solid waste;
(6) Rules and regulations pertaining to public swimming pools, spas, and recreational water parks (adopted by the department of public health and the county board of health and being chapter 511-3-5 as subsequently amended and updated), and policies of the county board of health pertaining to public swimming pools, spas, and recreational water parks;
(7) Rules and regulations pertaining to portable sanitation contractors (adopted by the department of public health and the county board of health and being chapter 511-3-6 as subsequently amended and updated), and policies of the county board of health pertaining to portable sanitation;
